+# 01: Reserve stock and look up a reservation
+
+**What to build:** The cart service can reserve stock for a cart in one warehouse and get back a Reservation describing exactly what was reserved. Each line reserves as many units as are available right now, up to what was asked for; lines with nothing available are left out. Reserved units stop being available to other carts and to directly placed orders. The reservation can be looked up later by its identifier. Expiry, retries, confirm and release come in later tickets; in this ticket a reservation simply stays active. See the spec (`spec.md` in this feature directory) and ADR-0001 (partial reservations).
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] `ReservationStatus` enum exists with members `ACTIVE`, `CONFIRMED`, `RELEASED`, `EXPIRED`, and a `Reservation` record exists with exactly the public fields `reservation_id`, `warehouse`, `items` (units reserved per SKU), `status`, `expires_at`, `order_id`; both are exported from the package root
+- [x] `ReservationNotFound`, `ReservationExpired`, `InvalidReservationState`, `IdempotencyConflict` exist and all subclass `InventoryError`
+- [x] `reserve(warehouse, items, idempotency_key)` returns an `ACTIVE` reservation with a unique identifier, `order_id` of `None`, and `expires_at` equal to the clock time at creation plus 20 minutes
+- [x] When enough stock is available, every requested line is reserved in full
+- [x] When a line is short, it reserves exactly what is available (e.g. 6 TEE requested, 5 available → 5 reserved), and the other lines are unaffected
+- [x] A line with nothing available is omitted from `items`, never shown with 0
+- [x] When no line can reserve anything, `reserve` raises `InsufficientStock` and no reservation is created
+- [x] Unknown warehouse → `UnknownWarehouse`, unknown SKU → `UnknownSku`, non-positive or non-integer quantity → `InvalidQuantity`, exactly as `place_order` validates; a rejected request reserves nothing, not even for its valid lines
+- [x] Empty `items` and an empty or blank idempotency key are rejected with an `InventoryError` (`InvalidOrder`)
+- [x] `get_reservation` returns the reservation; an unknown identifier raises `ReservationNotFound`
+- [x] `reserved(sku, warehouse)` returns the units held by active reservations for that SKU in that warehouse
+- [x] `available` is on-hand minus allocated minus reserved, never below zero; `allocated` still counts only placed orders
+- [x] `place_order` cannot take reserved units, and remains all-or-nothing
+- [x] A reservation in one warehouse does not change any figure in another warehouse; a reservation for one SKU does not change other SKUs
+- [x] All existing tests pass unchanged; new tests go through the public service API only
+
