+# 02: Safe retries with an idempotency key
+
+**What to build:** The cart service can retry `reserve` after a network failure without claiming stock twice. A repeat with the same idempotency key and the same request returns the original reservation; reusing a key for a different request is reported as a conflict. A reserve that failed leaves its key free, so the cart can try again once stock arrives. Matching is by what was requested, not by what ended up reserved. See the spec (`spec.md` in this feature directory).
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Reserve stock and look up a reservation)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] A repeated `reserve` with the same key, warehouse and requested items returns the same reservation (same `reservation_id`) and reserves no additional stock
+- [x] A repeated `reserve` does not change `expires_at`, even when the clock has moved on
+- [x] A partially filled reservation still matches on retry: the comparison is against the originally requested quantities, not the reserved `items`
+- [x] The order of items in the request does not affect matching
+- [x] Reusing a key with a different warehouse raises `IdempotencyConflict`
+- [x] Reusing a key with different SKUs or different quantities raises `IdempotencyConflict`
+- [x] A `reserve` that failed (`InsufficientStock`, unknown SKU or warehouse, bad quantity) leaves no trace, and a later `reserve` with the same key can succeed
+- [x] Keys are global: the same key cannot be bound to reservations in two different warehouses
+- [x] An invalid request reusing a bound key reports the validation error rather than the conflict
+- [x] The requested quantities stay internal; `Reservation` exposes no extra public fields
+
