+- [x] The reservation becomes `CONFIRMED` and its `order_id` is the new order's identifier
+- [x] `available` is the same immediately before and after confirmation; `reserved` drops and `allocated` rises by the same amount
+- [x] Confirm does not re-check availability
+- [x] Confirming a `CONFIRMED` reservation again returns the same order and creates no new order
+- [x] A repeated confirm still works after the 20 minutes have passed
+- [x] A repeated confirm after the order was cancelled or shipped returns that order in its current state, without error
+- [x] Confirming an `EXPIRED` reservation raises `ReservationExpired`, including at exactly `expires_at`
+- [x] Confirming an unknown identifier raises `ReservationNotFound`
+- [x] A `CONFIRMED` reservation never becomes `EXPIRED`
+- [x] A repeated `reserve` with the same key and request returns the reservation as `CONFIRMED`
+- [x] The resulting order ships and cancels like any other order; cancelling it frees its allocation and leaves the reservation `CONFIRMED`
