+# Reservations take what is available; orders stay all-or-nothing
+
+`reserve` holds as much of each line as is available right now, drops lines with nothing available, and fails only when no line can hold anything — whereas `place_order` remains all-or-nothing. This is deliberate: at checkout, "only 3 left, we've held them for you" converts better than an error. The cart detects the shortfall itself by comparing the reservation's `items` with what it asked for, so the reservation does not expose the requested quantities.
